> WinDOS users? What about Mac? OSX is a Unix; does it come with Nethack?
...

Not sure about the Linix distros these days, but OpenBSD has a port 
builder for NetHack that has to download the source when it's installed 
rather than having it pre-installed; there is also a precompiled NetHack 
package for OpenBSD, so users who install that way wouldn't be counted 
in the download stats.

MacOSX does not come with NetHack, though the Fink package system offers 
a pre-compiled NetHack package (which appears to also be used by 
darwinports) so those installs wouldn't be counted either.

